        <body>
            <div xml:id="d776">

                <pb facs="0808" n="494" xml:id="pg494"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 195.1/62</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Rio de Janeiro</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Burnell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate General</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Rio De Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                        ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                        notAfter="1914-09-22T02:20:00-05:00" notBefore="1914-09-21T00:00:00-03:00"
                            ><hi rendition="#italic">undated</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Received September 22, 1914, 2:20 a.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>The British Consul states that acting under instructions from the British
                    Legation he cannot until so instructed close register of steamer 
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Robert Dollar</hi>. British Legation is
                    awaiting instructions in the premises from London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Burnell</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
